  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Which of the following is the same as\n\n\\[\\frac{2 - 4 + 6 - 8 + 10 - 12 + 14}{3 - 6 + 9 - 12 + 15 - 18 + 21}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{14}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The numerator and denominator have the same alternating pattern, multiplied by 2 and 3 respectively. Let\n\\[\nS=1-2+3-4+5-6+7.\n\\]\nPairing adjacent terms gives \\(S=-1-1-1+7=4\\). The requested fraction is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{2S}{3S}=\\frac{8}{12}=\\boxed{\\frac23}.\n\\]\nThe denominator is \\(12\\ne0\\), so the cancellation is valid. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
